  "content": {
    "title": "NJ's Jake Thistle gives 'fired up' performance on 'American Idol'",
    "text": "Updated March 30, 2026, 11:31 p.m. ETParamus native Jake Thistle was back performing live on \"American Idol\" on Monday, March 30.Thistle got good news early in the episode that he made to the Final 14 after the Hawaii performances. The season began with 127 total contestants.However, two more performers were supposed to be cut before the two-hour live show ended on Monday. However, host Ryan Seacrest announced that due to the volume of votes they would not announce the elimination on Monday's show. He said \"American Idol\" has never done this before.The theme of the show was Songs of Faith. All 20 contestants backed up Lionel Richie and Luke Bryan on \"Jesus Is Love\" during an opening number on the show.When it came his solo turn, the 21-year-old singer-songwriter performed \"Have a Little Faith in Me\" by John Hiatt. The judges all responded positively to Thistle's performance.Ritchie said Jake \"got fired up.\"Carrie Underwood said, \"Your space is just so professional. I felt like I was at your show.\"Bryan commented: \"You were so comfortable\" like \"a seasoned entertainer.\"Host Ryan Seacrest asked Thistle what it feels like to be center stage and he said: \"It really feels incredible.\"Story continues below photo galleryThistle said he's gotten so close to the other contestants and he's grateful to share the stage with them. Then Seacrest said, \"I keep seeing Tom Cruise in your face,\" and Thistle responded, \"I'll take it.\" New episodes of \"American Idol\" air on Mondays at 8 p.m. on ABC. Episodes are available to stream on Hulu the following day.",
